  "text": "Hot coffee cools fast at first, then it crawls. Why? Your mug starts at ninety degrees in a twenty degree room. That gap is seventy degrees. Newton found the cooling rate tracks the gap. Every ten minutes, the gap halves: seventy, thirty five, seventeen and a half. Big gap, fast cooling. Small gap, slow cooling. It never drops below the room. That's Newton's law of cooling. Watch it again.",
